ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":160,"prev":162,"next":165,"titles":167,"firmware":78},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":12,"order":13,"path":14,"context":15,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":28,"procedures":90,"parameters":127,"related":128,"body":134,"sources":135,"official_url":32,"controls":146},"arrange.scenes","Scenes",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"scene","select scene","scene 10-99","clone scene","copy scene","paste scene","reset scene","arrange",30,"knowledge/manual/units/arrange/scenes.md",{"modes":16,"screens":17},[12],[],"A scene stores which pattern each track plays plus the mutes; a project has 99. In arrange, shift and a black key select one, and `shift + M1…M4` clone, copy, paste or reset.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[23,24,25],"1.0.29","1.0.45","1.1.0","1.1.15",null,[29,34,39,42,47,51,54,57,60,63,66,70,74,80,83,86],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"what","A project has 99 scenes. Each one remembers which pattern every track plays, together with the mutes.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/arrange#scenes","official",{"id":35,"text":36,"source":37,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":38},"mix-follows-pattern","Levels and pans are not kept per scene but travel with each pattern's sound, in tutorial videos on OS 1.0.x, although TE's guide counts the mix as part of the scene.","docs/research/65-video-tutorials.md#216-mixer","community-verified",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"length","A scene runs as long as its longest pattern.",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":45,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":46},"length-muted","Muted tracks do not count towards a scene's length; with a one-bar drum pattern unmuted and longer patterns muted, the scene is one bar (one video, narrated, OS 1.0.x). If every track is muted, all of them count.","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":50,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":27,"confidence":38},"length-modes","Since OS 1.1.0 a project setting picks how scene length is worked out; project files know three modes: longest (the default), shortest and time signature.","docs/research/10-xy-format.md#32-projectsettings-0x00000x0094",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"select","Holding `shift` and pressing a black key selects scenes 1–9, each key standing for its printed digit.",{"id":55,"text":56,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"select-high","Scenes 10–99 start with `shift + accidental 0` (the last black key), followed by the scene number typed on the black keys.",{"id":58,"text":59,"source":32,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"empty","Selecting an empty scene fills it with a copy of the current one, so a song can grow scene by scene.",{"id":61,"text":62,"source":32,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"clone-reset","`shift + M1` clones the current scene; `shift + M4` resets it, putting every track back on pattern 1.",{"id":64,"text":65,"source":32,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"copy-paste","`shift + M2` copies a scene and `shift + M3` pastes it into another.",{"id":67,"text":68,"source":69,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"midi","Over MIDI, on any channel, CC85 selects a scene at once and CC83 and CC84 step to the previous and the next scene.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/midi-references",{"id":71,"text":72,"source":73,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":38},"midi-zero","CC85 counts from zero, so value 0 selects scene 1 and value 98 scene 99.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#31-global-ccs",{"id":75,"text":76,"source":77,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":78,"confidence":79},"select-while-song","Selected while the song plays (`shift` and a black key, in arrange), a scene takes over at once, mid-bar, its patterns carrying on from the song's place in the bar; from then on the unit plays that scene over and over and the song stops moving on. This is how to loop one scene.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-28-night--songs-and-scenes-on-the-unit-owner-present-tes-agent-os-1133","1.1.33","verified",{"id":81,"text":82,"source":77,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":78,"confidence":79},"select-before-play","Picked while stopped (`shift` and its black key, in arrange), a scene is what play starts with instead of the song's first scene, and it repeats — twenty bars of scene 7 in a test on OS 1.1.33, where the song would have moved on to scene 6.",{"id":84,"text":85,"source":77,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":78,"confidence":79},"select-arrange-only","`shift` and the black keys pick scenes only in arrange mode.",{"id":87,"text":88,"source":89,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":78,"confidence":79},"footer","With `shift` held in arrange, the footer names `M1`…`M4` clone, copy, paste and reset, the scene actions.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#29-arrange-and-song-mode",[91,101,107,114],{"id":92,"goal":93,"preconditions":94,"steps":97,"result":27,"source":77,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":78,"confidence":79},"loop-one","Loop one scene while the song plays",[95,96],"arrange mode","playing",[98],{"keys":99,"note":100,"set":27},"shift + accidental","the scene to keep; it starts at once and then repeats, and the song stops moving on",{"id":52,"goal":102,"preconditions":103,"steps":104,"result":27,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"Select scene 1–9",[95],[105],{"keys":99,"note":106,"set":27},"the black key with the scene's digit",{"id":55,"goal":108,"preconditions":109,"steps":110,"result":27,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"Select a scene from 10 to 99",[95],[111],{"keys":112,"note":113,"set":27},"shift + accidental 0 → + accidentals","then type both digits; whether `shift` must stay down for